# Files Claude Code should not scan, index, or read directly.
# These are generated or vendored — excluding them cuts the file-watching load
# (mitigates the BSODs) and speeds up search. Shell commands (git, dotnet,
# npm, docker) are unaffected and can still use these paths.

# --- EF Core generated migration code (TRACKED in git, unlike everything
# else here). Each *.Designer.cs and the model snapshot is a full re-dump of
# the schema — 30 files, 3.3 MB, larger than docs/trackly-plan.md apiece, and
# never hand-edited. They swamp any grep for a column or table name.
# The hand-written Up()/Down() migration bodies stay readable.
**/Migrations/*.Designer.cs
**/Migrations/*ModelSnapshot.cs

# --- .NET build output ---
bin/
obj/
.vs/
artifacts/
TestResults/
packages/
*.binlog
*.nupkg
*.user
*.suo

# --- Node (both frontend/ and frontend-angular/) ---
node_modules/
.pnpm-store/
.yarn/cache/
.npm/
package-lock.json
yarn.lock
pnpm-lock.yaml

# --- Angular build + cache (frontend-angular/) ---
# .angular/cache is the Angular CLI / Vite build cache — the largest generated
# tree in the repo and pure churn. out-tsc is `ng test`/tsc emit.
.angular/
out-tsc/
.nx/
bazel-out/
*.tsbuildinfo
.ng-build-cache/

# --- Bundler / test output (shared) ---
dist/
dist-ssr/
build/
.vite/
coverage/
.nyc_output/
__screenshots__/
playwright-report/
test-results/

# --- Stylesheet caches ---
.sass-cache/
*.css.map
*.js.map

# --- Version control internals (use git commands, never read directly) ---
.git/

# --- IDE / OS cruft ---
.idea/
.history/
*.swp
*.sublime-workspace
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db

# --- Logs ---
logs/
*.log
